                                                                                
 Usage: opentide validate query [OPTIONS]                                       
                                                                                
 Check rule queries offline with the analysis engine, or on the tenants         
 (--live).                                                                      
                                                                                
 Offline, the engine reports the queries the platform would reject, as          
 `opentide validate` does; `opentide lint` reports their style.                 
                                                                                
╭─ Options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ --platform             PLATFORM    Check this platform's queries. Offline,   │
│                                    default every platform the engine parses: │
│                                    carbon_black_cloud,                       │
│                                    defender_for_endpoint, elastic, sentinel, │
│                                    splunk, sysdig. --live needs one of:      │
│                                    carbon_black_cloud,                       │
│                                    defender_for_endpoint, elastic, sentinel, │
│                                    sentinel_one, splunk                      │
│ --strategy             <str>       Check only rules a run with this strategy │
│                                    deploys (repeatable), on the tenants that │
│                                    accept it. Default: PREVIEW and RELEASE   │
│ --wide                             Check every status strategy but           │
│                                    DISABLEMENT and DELETION (--live)         │
│ --live                             Check the queries on the platform's       │
│                                    tenants (needs credentials)               │
│ --changed                          Check only the rule files this run        │
│                                    changed: the pull or merge request, the   │
│                                    push, or outside CI the last commit (the  │
│                                    files deploy reads)                       │
│ --file                 <str>       Check only this rule file, or this query  │
│                                    file (.kql, .spl, .esql, .eql, .kuery,    │
│                                    .lucene, .falco) offline (repeatable)     │
│ --uuid                 <str>       Check only the rule with this UUID        │
│                                    (repeatable)                              │
│ --strict                           Fail on warnings too                      │
│ --queries              error|warn  How a rejected query is reported offline: │
│                                    error (the default) or warn               │
│ --check-timeout        SECONDS     Seconds each query may take on a tenant   │
│                                    before its check fails (--live; default:  │
│                                    OPENTIDE_QUERY_CHECK_TIMEOUT, else 120)   │
│ --help                             Show this message and exit.               │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

 Examples
   $ opentide validate query
   $ opentide validate query --platform splunk --changed
   $ opentide validate query --file hunting/lsass.kql
   $ opentide validate query --platform sentinel --live
